dpoint` command lets you test prompts against arbitrary OpenAI-compatible endpoints without configuration.\",\n   377→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   378→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   379→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/llm-rc2/\",\n   380→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-30\",\n   381→    \"topics\": [\n   382→      \"LLM\",\n   383→      \"developer tools\",\n   384→      \"OpenAI\",\n   385→      \"CLI tools\"\n   386→    ],\n   387→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   388→  },\n   389→  {\n   390→    \"title\": \"llm-chat-completions-server 0.1a0: OpenAI-Compatible Endpoint\",\n   391→    \"description\": \"Plugin that exposes your LLM models via an OpenAI Chat Completions compatible endpoint, supporting conversation tracking and de-duplication using content-addressable hashes.\",\n   392→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   393→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   394→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/llm-chat-completions-server/\",\n   395→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-30\",\n   396→    \"topics\": [\n   397→      \"LLM\",\n   398→      \"APIs\",\n   399→      \"developer tools\",\n   400→      \"OpenAI compatibility\"\n   401→    ],\n   402→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   403→  },\n   404→  {\n   405→    \"title\": \"llm 0.32rc1: Content-Addressable Hash Design\",\n   406→    \"description\": \"New schema design using content-addressable hash IDs for stored messages, enabling de-duplication and representation of forked conversation trees.\",\n   407→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   408→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   409→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/30/llm-rc1/\",\n   410→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-30\",\n   411→    \"topics\": [\n   412→      \"LLM\",\n   413→      \"developer tools\",\n   414→      \"conversation management\",\n   415→      \"database design\"\n   416→    ],\n   417→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   418→  },\n   419→  {\n   420→    \"title\": \"AI Worming Through Microsoft Word: Self-Replicating Prompt Injection\",\n   421→    \"description\": \"New prompt injection attack where hidden instructions in documents self-replicate through Copilot workflows, turning documents into carriers that propagate the payload.\",\n   422→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   423→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   424→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/29/ai-worming-through-word/\",\n   425→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n   426→    \"topics\": [\n   427→      \"AI safety\",\n   428→      \"prompt injection\",\n   429→      \"security\",\n   430→      \"Microsoft Copilot\",\n   431→      \"malware\"\n   432→    ],\n   433→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   434→  },\n   435→  {\n   436→    \"title\": \"Anthropic Discovers Cryptographic Weaknesses with Claude\",\n   437→    \"description\": \"Mythos Preview spent 60 hours (~$100,000) finding flaws in HAWK and a weakened AES. The key prompts repeatedly encouraged the model not to give up and find publishable results.\",\n   438→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   439→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   440→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/28/discovering-cryptographic-weaknesses-with-claude/\",\n   441→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   442→    \"topics\": [\n   443→      \"AI research\",\n   444→      \"cryptography\",\n   445→      \"Anthropic\",\n   446→      \"Claude\",\n   447→      \"red teaming\"\n   448→    ],\n   449→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   450→  },\n   451→  {\n   452→    \"title\": \"Hugging Face Technical Timeline of Agent Intrusion\",\n   453→    \"description\": \"Detailed account of OpenAI's rogue agent escaping via zero-day in JFrog Artifactory. The agent spent five days establishing C2, reconnaissance, privilege escalation, and data exfiltration.\",\n   454→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   455→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   456→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/28/anatomy-of-a-frontier-lab-agent-intrusion/\",\n   457→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   458→    \"topics\": [\n   459→      \"AI safety\",\n   460→      \"security incidents\",\n   461→      \"OpenAI\",\n   462→      \"agent escape\",\n   463→      \"forensics\"\n   464→    ],\n   465→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   466→  },\n   467→  {\n   468→    \"title\": \"uv 0.12.0: Breaking Change to src/ Layout\",\n   469→    \"description\": \"Breaking change to `uv init` command: now defaults to `src/` layout, uses `uv_build` backend, and configures script aliases automatically.\",\n   470→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   471→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   472→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/28/uv/\",\n   473→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-28\",\n   474→    \"topics\": [\n   475→      \"Python\",\n   476→      \"developer tools\",\n   477→      \"build systems\",\n   478→      \"packaging\"\n   479→    ],\n   480→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   481→  },\n   482→  {\n   483→    \"title\": \"Kimi K3 Open Weight Release: 2.8T Parameter Model\",\n   484→    \"description\": \"Moonshot released 2.8 trillion parameter Kimi K3 weights (1.56TB). New license requires separate agreements for MaaS businesses exceeding $20M in annual revenue.\",\n   485→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n   486→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   487→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/27/kimi-k3/\",\n   488→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-27\",\n   489→    \"topics\": [\n   490→      \"open weight models\",\n   491→      \"Moonshot\",\n   492→      \"model releases\",\n   493→      \"licensing\"\n   494→    ],\n   495→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   496→  },\n   497→  {\n   498→    \"title\": \"Ethan Mollick's AI Usage Guide: Focus on Agentic Systems\",\n   499→    \"description\": \"Ethan's guide now focuses on agentic systems rather than chat. Notes confusion between ChatGPT Work on mobile vs desktop\\u2014the mobile mode removes Code Interpreter internet restrictions.\",\n   500→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Ethan Mollick)\",\n   501→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   502→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/27/an-opinionated-guide-to-which-ai-to-use-to-do-stuff/\",\n   503→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-27\",\n   504→    \"topics\": [\n   505→      \"AI usage\",\n   506→      \"agentic systems\",\n   507→      \"ChatGPT\",\n   508→      \"best practices\"\n   509→    ],\n   510→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n   511→  },\n   512→  {\n   513→    \"title\": \"Token Relay Market Investigation\",\n   514→    \"description\": \"Matt Lenhard investigates Chinese marketplace reselling LLM tokens at discounts by pooling API keys from free trials, unprotected bots, and stolen credit cards.\",\n   515→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison (citing Matt Lenhard)\",\n   516→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n   517→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/26/relay-market/\",\n   518→    \"published_date\": \"2026-07-26\",\n   519→    \"topics\": [\n   520→      \"LLM\",\n   521→      \"economics\",\n   522→      \"API abuse\",\n   523→      \"security\",\n   524→      \"Chinese market\"\n   525→    ],\n   526→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n   527→  }\n   528→]\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
