-description\">\n   673→                        User-centric system prompt auditing framework for LLM applications, focusing on evaluation and auditing capabilities.\n   674→                    </div>\n   675→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Xiangning Lin et al. | 2026-07-31</div>\n   676→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   677→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n   678→                        <span class=\"tag\">auditing</span>\n   679→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n   680→                    </div>\n   681→                </div>\n   682→\n   683→                <div class=\"item\">\n   684→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   685→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-arxiv\">ARXIV</span>\n   686→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28609\">OSReward: Standardized Evaluation for Computer-Use</a>\n   687→                    </div>\n   688→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   689→                        Standardized evaluation for cross-platform computer-use reward models to assess AI agents interacting with operating systems.\n   690→                    </div>\n   691→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Qiushi Sun et al. | 2026-07-31</div>\n   692→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   693→                        <span class=\"tag\">evaluation</span>\n   694→                        <span class=\"tag\">benchmarks</span>\n   695→                        <span class=\"tag\">computer-use</span>\n   696→                    </div>\n   697→                </div>\n   698→\n   699→                <div class=\"item\">\n   700→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   701→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-arxiv\">ARXIV</span>\n   702→                        <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.28103\">MIND: Memory Injection Defense for LLM Agents</a>\n   703→                    </div>\n   704→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   705→                        Lightweight and effective memory injection defense for LLM agents via intent-aware information bottleneck to protect against prompt injection attacks.\n   706→                    </div>\n   707→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Dongyi Liu et al. | 2026-07-31</div>\n   708→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   709→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n   710→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   711→                        <span class=\"tag\">defense</span>\n   712→                    </div>\n   713→                </div>\n   714→\n   715→                <div class=\"item\">\n   716→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   717→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n   718→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/31/stateless-mcp/\">MCP 2.0 - Major Specification Update</a>\n   719→                    </div>\n   720→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   721→                        The MCP 2.0 specification launches as 'the most significant change to the MCP spec since it first launched.' Simon also released mcp-explorer and datasette-mcp tools.\n   722→                    </div>\n   723→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Simon Willison | 2026-07-31</div>\n   724→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   725→                        <span class=\"tag\">MCP</span>\n   726→                        <span class=\"tag\">standards</span>\n   727→                        <span class=\"tag\">specifications</span>\n   728→                    </div>\n   729→                </div>\n   730→\n   731→                <div class=\"item\">\n   732→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   733→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n   734→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/31/smevals/\">smevals Evaluation Framework</a>\n   735→                    </div>\n   736→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   737→                        New tool for running eval suites across different model configurations. Uses vocabulary of evals, tasks, configs, runs, graders, and checks for systematic model evaluation.\n   738→                    </div>\n   739→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Simon Willison | 2026-07-31</div>\n   740→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   741→                        <span class=\"tag\">evaluation</span>\n   742→                        <span class=\"tag\">testing</span>\n   743→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n   744→                    </div>\n   745→                </div>\n   746→\n   747→                <div class=\"item\">\n   748→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   749→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n   750→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/31/deepseek-v4-flash-0731/\">DeepSeek V4 Flash 0731 Release</a>\n   751→                    </div>\n   752→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   753→                        New 304B parameter model offering 'substantially enhanced agentic capabilities' at $0.14/$0.27 per million tokens. High reasoning mode needed for complex image tasks.\n   754→                    </div>\n   755→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Simon Willison | 2026-07-31</div>\n   756→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   757→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM</span>\n   758→                        <span class=\"tag\">model releases</span>\n   759→                        <span class=\"tag\">pricing</span>\n   760→                    </div>\n   761→                </div>\n   762→\n   763→                <div class=\"item\">\n   764→                    <div class=\