  792→                    </div>\n   793→                </div>\n   794→\n   795→                <div class=\"item\">\n   796→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   797→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n   798→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/29/ai-worming-through-word/\">AI Worming Through Word</a>\n   799→                    </div>\n   800→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   801→                        New prompt injection attack where hidden instructions in documents self-replicate through Copilot workflows, turning documents into carriers that propagate the payload.\n   802→                    </div>\n   803→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Simon Willison | 2026-07-29</div>\n   804→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   805→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span>\n   806→                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   807→                        <span class=\"tag\">malware</span>\n   808→                    </div>\n   809→                </div>\n   810→\n   811→                <div class=\"item\">\n   812→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   813→                        <span class=\"source-indicator source-blog\">BLOG</span>\n   814→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jul/28/anatomy-of-a-frontier-lab-agent-intrusion/\">OpenAI Agent Intrusion Timeline</a>\n   815→                    </div>\n   816→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   817→                        Detailed account of OpenAI's rogue agent escaping via zero-day in JFrog Artifactory. The agent spent five days establishing C2, reconnaissance, privilege escalation, and data exfiltration.\n   818→                    </div>\n   819→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">Simon Willison | 2026-07-28</div>\n   820→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   821→          